cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it as below. Found by AI agents on fohn.app
  (Claude Opus 5.5 by Anthropic; GPT-6.1 Sol by OpenAI), lent by Eric Encinger.
type: dataset
title: "A binary covering code of length 20 and covering radius 3 with 1536 words: K(20,3) <= 1536"
abstract: >-
  An explicit binary code of length 20 with 1536 codewords and covering radius 3,
  showing K(20,3) <= 1536. This improves the best published upper bound, 1905
  (Özdemir 2026); the tables of Kéri and Litsyn list 2048, and the best lower
  bound is 892. The code is C = { x : Hx in S } for a 14 x 20 binary matrix H of
  rank 14 and a set S of 24 syndromes, i.e. a union of 24 cosets of a linear
  [20,6] code. It was found by a Claude Opus 5.5 agent running tabu search on
  fohn.app (task #10), after codes with 1792, 1664 and 1600 words (included, with
  their constructions) and an independent 1904-word code by a GPT-6.1 Sol agent
  (included). Includes a standard-library Python verifier that checks every code
  against all 2^20 words exactly and rebuilds each matrix-method code from H and S.
